      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "a2-cooking-recipes-01",
        "slug": "a2-recipe-imperatives",
        "title": "Imperatives for recipe steps",
        "rule_summary": "Recipes commonly use the base verb without a subject to give clear instructions.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در دستور پخت معمولاً شکل ساده فعل بدون فاعل برای دستور دادن استفاده می‌شود؛ مثل Chop, Add, Mix."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "Chop the onion.",
            "fa": "پیاز را خرد کن."
          },
          {
            "en": "Add two eggs.",
            "fa": "دو تخم‌مرغ اضافه کن."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "A2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_a2_recipe_sequence",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "a2-cooking-recipes-02",
        "slug": "a2-recipe-sequence",
        "title": "Sequence a recipe",
        "rule_summary": "Use first, then, next, after that, and finally to make recipe steps easy to follow.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "برای مرتب کردن مراحل دستور پخت از first، then، next، after that و finally استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "First, boil the water. Then add the pasta.",
            "fa": "اول آب را بجوشان. بعد پاستا را اضافه کن."
          },
          {
            "en": "Finally, add the sauce.",
            "fa": "در آخر سس را اضافه کن."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "A2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
